      {
        "id": 119929,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-02T14:51:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I don't think there are official rankings, but I'll take a stab at it.</p><p>This is based solely on my impression of new players being able to handle playing the character competently, mostly the more complex the options are the higher they rank.</p><p>FYI: I think Wraith and Bunker are the best two characters to learn the game with: &nbsp;Between the two they cover the whole gambit of mechanics really well. &nbsp;I like to give a new player one, then have them play the other next. &nbsp;If they understand both of them they are pretty well set.</p><p>Level 1:</p><p>Legacy</p><p>Bunker</p><p>Omnitron-V</p><p>Wraith&nbsp;</p><p>Level 2:</p><p><span>Beacon</span></p><p><span>Unity</span></p><p><span>Operative</span></p><p><span>Tachyon</span></p><p>Ra</p><p>Citizen Dawn</p><p>Level 3:</p><p>Absolute Zero</p><p>Baron Blade</p><p>Visionary</p><p>Level 4:</p><p>Ambuscade</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Proletariat</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:53:15.885Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
