        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I don&#39;t think there are official rankings, but I&#39;ll take a stab at it.</p><p>This is based solely on my impression of new players being able to handle playing the character competently, mostly the more complex the options are the higher they rank.</p><p>FYI: I think Wraith and Bunker are the best two characters to learn the game with: &nbsp;Between the two they cover the whole gambit of mechanics really well. &nbsp;I like to give a new player one, then have them play the other next. &nbsp;If they understand both of them they are pretty well set.</p><p><u>Level 1:</u></p><p>Legacy</p><p>Bunker</p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Omnitron-V</p><p>Wraith&nbsp;</p><p><u style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Level 2:</u></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Beacon</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Unity</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Operative</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Tachyon</span></p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Ra</p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Citizen Dawn</p><p><u>Level 3:</u></p><p>Absolute Zero</p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Baron Blade</p><p>Visionary</p><p><u style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Level 4:</u></p><p>Ambuscade</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-size: 13px; line-height: 20px;\">Proletariat</p>",
